WEBVTT

00:00:07.444 --> 00:00:09.683
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> <b>Girl by O. Henry</b>

00:00:34.258 --> 00:00:36.220
<v><b>Detective:</b></v> I’ve found where she lives.

00:00:39.757 --> 00:00:40.600
Here’s the address.

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.102
She moved there a week ago.

00:00:48.995 --> 00:00:50.240
I can follow her if you want.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.980
It will only cost you $7 a day and expenses…

00:00:58.207 --> 00:00:59.025
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> No, thank you.

00:00:59.702 --> 00:01:01.135
I only wanted the address.

00:01:02.124 --> 00:01:02.906
How much is it?

00:01:03.625 --> 00:01:05.510
<v><b>Detective:</b></v> One day’s work, ten dollars.

00:01:23.004 --> 00:01:27.050
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Then Hartley left his office and took a tram to Broadway.

00:01:28.308 --> 00:01:33.841
After walking a short distance he arrived at the building that he was looking for.

00:01:35.364 --> 00:01:37.825
He went up the stairs into her apartment,

00:01:38.682 --> 00:01:41.074
and saw her standing by the window.

00:01:43.391 --> 00:01:45.634
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> Vivienne, you didn’t answer my last letter.

00:01:46.707 --> 00:01:50.893
It took me a week to find your new address! Why didn’t you answer me?

00:01:51.554 --> 00:01:55.025
You knew I was waiting to see you and hear from you.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:00.401
<v><b>Vivienne:</b></v> Mr Hartley, I don’t know what to say to you.

00:02:01.289 --> 00:02:04.571
I understand all the advantages of your offer,

00:02:05.286 --> 00:02:10.469
and sometimes I feel sure that I could be happy with you.

00:02:11.504 --> 00:02:15.542
But, then sometimes I am less sure.

00:02:17.252 --> 00:02:24.857
I was born a city girl, and I am not sure that I would enjoy living a quiet life in the suburbs.

00:02:25.312 --> 00:02:28.158
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> My dear girl, you will have everything that you want.

00:02:28.666 --> 00:02:32.061
You can come to the city for the theatre, for shopping,

00:02:32.869 --> 00:02:35.024
and to visit your friends as often as you want.

00:02:38.878 --> 00:02:39.762
You can trust me,

00:02:42.152 --> 00:02:42.708
can’t you?

00:02:44.391 --> 00:02:48.917
<v><b>Vivienne:</b></v> I can trust you completely, I know you are the kindest of men,

00:02:49.022 --> 00:02:52.697
and that the girl who you get will be very lucky.

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:57.419
I heard all about you when I was at the Montgomerys’.

00:02:57.847 --> 00:03:02.129
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> Ha ha! I remember so well the evening I first saw you at the Montgomerys’.

00:03:03.244 --> 00:03:04.801
I will never forget that dinner.

00:03:07.418 --> 00:03:09.414
Come on, Vivienne, promise me.

00:03:10.646 --> 00:03:11.534
I want you.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:15.243
Nobody else will ever give you such a happy home.

00:03:18.766 --> 00:03:24.104
Tell me, Vivienne, is there…is there someone else?

00:03:24.982 --> 00:03:31.040
<v><b>Vivienne:</b></v> You shouldn’t ask that, Mr Hartley, but I will tell you.

00:03:31.593 --> 00:03:36.867
There is one other person…but I haven’t promised him anything.

00:03:37.518 --> 00:03:39.719
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> Vivienne, you must be mine.

00:03:41.315 --> 00:03:43.386
<v><b>Vivienne:</b></v> Do you think for one moment,

00:03:43.387 --> 00:03:46.843
that I could come to your home while Héloise is there?